{ Your kings face each other down the e column, and it is his move. Whatever he does with it, you will have to answer exactly. } 1... Kd8 { He steps aside to d8 rather than face you. That is his waiting move: find the reply that keeps the opposition. } 2. Kf3 { You leave a file between the kings. Copying his move would lose the timing. [%cal Ge2f3] } (2. Kd2 { Another good square, d2. The result stays with you. } 2... Ke7 { Also winning. Your king still preserves the distant opposition from here. [%cal Bd8e7] }) (2. Kf2 { Your king's route through f2 changes the result. } 2... Kd7 3. Kf3 3... Kd6 4. Kf4 4... Kd5 { The result has changed: this loses the distant opposition you fought for. [%cal Rd6d5] }) (2. Kd3 { You follow his king, but he can take the opposition. } 2... Kd7 3. Ke3 3... Ke7 4. Kd3 4... Kd7 { This move drops the opposition, and the result has changed. [%cal Re7d7] }) (2. Ke3 { You walk straight up, but Black can take the opposition. } 2... Ke7 3. Kf3 3... Kf7 4. Ke3 4... Ke7 { The result changes here, because his king takes the opposition instead. [%cal Rf7e7] }) 2... Ke7 { His king returns. How can you restore the direct opposition? } 3. Ke3 { Your king holds e3 with his king stuck on e7, three rows apart on the same column, and it is his turn. He must give ground before you do. [%cal Gf3e3] } (3. Kg3 { Try g3, and the result flips against you. } 3... Ke6 4. Kf4 4... Kf6 5. Ke4 5... Ke6 { You give up the opposition this way, and the result has changed. [%cal Rf6e6] }) (3. Ke4 { Your king can also try e4, but that changes the result. } 3... Ke6 4. Kd4 4... Kd6 5. Ke4 5... Ke6 { The result has changed. The opposition slips to his king now. [%cal Rd6e6] }) (3. Kf4 { The f4 square looks natural for your king, but it changes the result. } 3... Kf6 4. Ke4 4... Ke6 5. Kd4 5... Kd6 { This square lets him seize the opposition, and the result changes. [%cal Re6d6] }) (3. Kg2 { The g2 square is tempting, but the result changes there. } 3... Ke6 4. Kf2 4... Kd5 5. Kf3 5... Kc4 { The result has changed: the opposition needed to stay yours. [%cal Rd5c4] }) 1-0


