{ You are a pawn down and that pawn can be captured. Hold the draw: first make sure your king will not lose the race. } 2. Kg2 { Your king steps closer before taking. The timing, not the free pawn, comes first. [%cal Gh1g2] } (2. f4 { This pawn's route through f4 changes the result. } 2... exf4 3. Kh2 3... g3+ 4. Kh3 4... Kd2 { The result has changed: your king needed one more step closer before the race began. [%cal Rd1d2] }) (2. fxg4 { A free pawn is tempting. Your king has not gained the move it needs. } 2... e4 3. Kg2 3... e3 4. Kf3 4... Kd2 { The e pawn wins the race. Move your king closer before capturing. [%cal Rd1d2] }) (2. Kg1 { Your king can also try g1, but that changes the result. } 2... gxf3 3. Kf2 3... e4 4. Ke3 4... Ke1 { This starts the pawn race too early, and the result has changed. [%cal Rd1e1] }) (2. Kh2 { The h2 square looks natural for your king, but it changes the result. } 2... gxf3 3. Kg3 3... Ke2 4. Kg4 4... e4 { The result changes here. Your king is a tempo short in the race that follows. [%cal Re5e4] }) 2... Kd2 { His king steps away. Can you now take without falling behind? } 3. fxg4 { Your king on g2 is close enough now, so the pawn on g4 is yours. Both sides have a runner. [%cal Gf3g4] } (3. Kf2 { Stepping to f2 changes the result instead of keeping it. } 3... gxf3 4. Kxf3 4... Kd3 5. Kf2 5... e4 { Racing now instead of improving your king first changes the result. [%cal Re5e4] }) (3. Kg3 { Your king heading to g3 throws the result away. } 3... gxf3 4. Kxf3 4... Kd3 5. Kf2 5... e4 { The result has changed: his e pawn wins the race this way. [%cal Re5e4] }) (3. f4 { The pawn to f4 looks fine, but it changes the result. } 3... exf4 4. Kf2 4... Kc1 5. Ke2 5... Kc2 { This skips the improving move your king needed, and the result changes. [%cal Rc1c2] }) (3. Kg1 { The square g1 seems fine, but the result changes here. } 3... gxf3 4. Kf2 4... e4 5. Kg3 5... Ke2 { The result has changed. The race starts one move too soon. [%cal Rd2e2] }) 3... e4 { His pawn sets off down the e column. Only one move of yours keeps up with it. } 4. g5 { Your pawn goes at once. A king move would cost a step, and in a race a step is everything. [%tail] [%cal Gg4g5] } (4. Kf2 { You turn to chase his e pawn, but chasing costs moves you cannot spare. } 4... e3+ 5. Kf3 5... e2 { The pawn on e2 is one step from a queen and your king cannot get near it. Your own pawn never started. [%cal Re2e1] }) (4. Kg3 { A step forward with the king, and the pawn on g4 loses its head start. } 4... e3 5. Kf3 5... e2 { His e pawn is on the edge of queening while yours still sits on g4. The race is lost. [%cal Re2e1] }) 4... e3 5. g6 5... e2 6. g7 6... e1=Q 7. g8=Q { Both pawns turn into queens, yours on g8 and his on e1. Neither side can win that, so the game is a draw. [%csl Gg8] } 1-0


